{
  "title": "Whiteboard Desktop: three-minute tour",
  "document": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "markdown": "# Whiteboard Desktop: three-minute tour\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "title": "Welcome",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "markdown": "A whiteboard is a guided, interactive explanation of a code change. Code,\ndiffs, and diagrams live in one document.\n"
        },
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "markdown": "### Your keybindings\n\nChoose your editor keys. Whiteboard highlights the active choice and uses its\nexisting extension and reload flow for Vim, Emacs, and Sublime Text.\n"
        },
        {
          "type": "tutorial",
          "kind": "keymap"
        },
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "markdown": "### Read code like your editor\n\nThe editor below is live. Hover a symbol to see its type. **Go to\nDefinition** and **Find References** use the same keys as your editor.\n"
        },
        {
          "type": "code_peek",
          "source": "head/src/orders/order-service.ts#L13-L29",
          "caption": "Order service creates the order"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "title": "Diffs and lenses",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "markdown": "The **Diff** tab shows the whole change between the pinned base and head.\ndiffr folds unchanged structure so you read only what moved; select a fold to\nexpand it.\n"
        },
        {
          "type": "tutorial",
          "kind": "view",
          "view": "diff",
          "label": "Open the diff"
        },
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "markdown": "**Lenses** split a change into the parts that matter. Select a lens to\nfilter the diff to just those lines. Mark lines viewed and the remaining\ncounts go down.\n\nAI summaries for folded code are opt-in under **Settings → Diff display and\nAI summaries**.\n"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
